## 7. What would make this record ACCEPTED

An independent reviewer can start here, take any accepted source form from
section 4, trace it to exactly one fact producer in section 3, and then to every
consumer.

**The negative half must NOT be stated absolutely.** The earlier revision
required the reviewer to "find NO consumer deriving the result from an AST type
or printed text". That is unachievable as written, because **four such
re-derivations are already known** (CORRECTION 7: `nilMergeChainNonOptional`
:2048 consumed at :4776/:4879; closure declarations at :1203 and :5525-the-declaration (delegation :5524); switch
re-targeting at :5508-5515; `platformModuleCall` at :4349-4355). Demanding their
absence would make the record unpassable by construction.

The achievable condition is: **every known re-derivation is either eliminated or
individually ruled on**, each ruling recorded against the fact it affects - not a
claim that none exist. A focused fixture passing remains NOT acceptance.

## 8. What this record does NOT prove

It does not prove the mechanism is correct; it records who owns which fact and
where it is consumed. It does not cover the four unresolved producer families.
It is not a regression result. It has not been independently reviewed yet.
